ponse_pipeline_refactor.py\n│   ├── test_response_semantics.py\n│   ├── test_resume_after_forced_plaintext_completion_project.py\n│   ├── test_reuse_goal_refinement_and_prompt_budget.py\n│   ├── test_runtime_recovery_fixes.py\n│   ├── test_search_tools._py\n│   ├── test_session_manager._py\n│   ├── test_smoke_user_flow._py\n│   ├── test_state_machine._py\n│   ├── test_think_and_action_policy_fixes.py\n│   ├── test_tools_comprehensive._py\n│   ├── test_truncation._py\n│   ├── test_tui_ui._py\n│   ├── test_vertexai_provider.py\n│   └── test_visible_text.py\n├── .bumpversion.toml\n├── .codex\n├── .gitignore\n├── AGENTS.md\n├── Makefile\n├── README.md\n├── Test.kt\n├── agent.py\n├── angelica\n├── angelica.spec\n├── backup.exclude\n├── build.sh\n├── concat_into.py\n├── debug.log.1\n├── debug.log.2\n├── debug.log.3\n├── debug.log.4\n├── debug.log.5\n├── debug_repro.py\n├── debug_selection.py\n├── hello_world.py\n├── interval_notifier.py\n├── message.sh\n├── path.txt\n├── pyinstaller.log\n├── pytest.ini\n├── python_markdown_example.md\n├── requirements.txt\n├── screens.py\n├── script1.py\n├── sources.txt\n├── test_create_file.py\n├── test_create_file_real.py\n├── test_diff_preview.py\n├── test_format.py\n├── test_tool_call.py\n├── textarea_debug.log\n├── tui.css\n├── tui.py\n├── довільний_текст.txt\n└── привіт_світ.txt\n\nNavigation guidance: prefer `read_file_skeleton` to inspect structure cheaply and obtain symbol line ranges before using broader or larger reads. When you already know the symbol target, prefer `extract_symbol` over repeated search + chunk hunting, and use `read_chunk` only for exact line-ranged follow-up. Under MODIFY, investigation remains valid until edit-readiness is achieved.\n\n## SUBGOAL BOARD XML PROTOCOL\nThe subgoal board belongs to the CURRENT ACTIVE INTENT. Do not repeat intent_id in subgoal tags.\nEmit flat top-level <subgoal ...> XML tags. Do not wrap them inside a container tag.\nEach subgoal tag is an independent mutation applied to the current active intent subgoal board.\nSubgoal tags are optional for trivial one-step work, but required when decomposition is useful.\nCanonical syntax:\n- <subgoal action=\"create\" id=\"sg_1\" status=\"todo|in_progress|done|blocked\">Meaningful subgoal</subgoal>\n- <subgoal action=\"modify\" id=\"sg_1\" status=\"todo|in_progress|done|blocked\">Updated title</subgoal>\n- <subgoal action=\"mark_done\" id=\"sg_1\" evidence=\"tool:read_file path.py lines 10-20\" />\n- <subgoal action=\"mark_todo\" id=\"sg_1\" />\n- <subgoal action=\"mark_in_progress\" id=\"sg_1\" />\n- <subgoal action=\"mark_blocked\" id=\"sg_1\" reason=\"Short blocking reason\" />\n- <subgoal action=\"remove\" id=\"sg_1\" reason=\"Why this is no longer needed\" />\n- <subgoal action=\"reorder\" id=\"sg_3\" after=\"sg_1\" />\n- <subgoal action=\"clear_all\" />\nRules:\n- Each id must be stable.\n- Each subgoal must be a meaningful subproblem, not a trivial tool click.\n- Prefer a few strong subgoals over many micro-steps.\n- Use memory tags to explain WHY the subgoal board changed; use subgoal tags to change the board state.\n\n\n## MEMORY BOARD PROTOCOL\nMemory tags are part of working continuity, not decoration.\nSupported tags:\n- <fact scope=\"intent|session|project\">...</fact>\n- <finding scope=\"intent|session|project\">...</finding>\n- <decision scope=\"intent|session|project\">...</decision>\n- <preference scope=\"intent|session|project\">...</preference>\n- <progress scope=\"intent\">...</progress>\n- <path scope=\"intent|session|project\">...</path>\n- <memory_review status=\"no_change\" scope=\"intent\" />\n- <memory_update_done />\n\nDURABLE STATE CHECKPOINT RULE:\n- Durable-state checkpointing is mandatory.\n- Every step must run this cycle in order: Sufficiency Check -> State Review -> Memory/Subgoal Update -> Action or Answer.\n- You MUST emit memory tags and/or formal plan tags:\n  after every <think>,\n  after every meaningful reasoning result,\n  after every tool result that materially changes what is known, what should be done next, or what is already completed,\n  and after every user input that changes the active goal interpretation, plan structure, priorities, constraints, or durable memory relevance.\n- Put the tags immediately after </think> and before any <action> or plain-text continuation.\n- End the memory/subgoal review block for the step with <memory_update_done />.\n- If the review found no memory/subgoal mutation to emit, output <memory_update_done /> anyway after the review.\n- If the review found no durable mutation but you still need to acknowledge the review explicitly before a risky action, you may emit <memory_review status=\"no_change\" scope=\"intent\" /> immediately before <memory_update_done />.\n- When in doubt, checkpoint more rather than less.\n- Loss of durable operational state after history compression is a critical failure.\n\nTag selection:\n- Use <fact> for information directly verified by tool output, code, or runtime state already visible in history.\n- Use <finding> for conclusions, interpretations, suspected behavior, or any statement that is not directly quoted or directly observable from tool output.\n- Use <decision> for durable chosen rules, strategy choices, or explicit working decisions that should survive compression.\n- Use <progress> for milestone-level continuation state.\n- Use <path> for file paths, directory paths, module paths, or exact edit/inspection surfaces that are likely to matter later in the same work.\n- Use <preference> only for durable preference-like guidance that actually matters later.\n- Do NOT write plans, subgoals, next-step lists, or pending task decompositions into the memory board.\n- Do NOT collapse formal subgoal mutations into <progress> or <decision>; use the dedicated <subgoal ...> XML tags for subgoal state changes.\n- If the content is a plan, step list, next action, or task decomposition, it belongs in <subgoal ...>, not in memory tags.\n- If a newly discovered path i